
===== 2026-08-01T17:58:45.562592+00:00 ['run', 'Please set up an hourly recurring automation that triages new customer inquiries from the local support API at http://127.0.0.1:8128.\n\nHow it works: GET http://127.0.0.1:8128/batches/last returns {"last_seq": N} — the highest inquiry seq already triaged (0 if none yet). GET http://127.0.0.1:8128/inquiries?after=N returns the next inquiries with seq > N (up to 200), each with fields: seq (int) and text (str).\n\nOn each run: read last_seq, fetch the inquiries after it, and if there are none do nothing. Otherwise classify each inquiry into exactly one category based on what the customer needs: "refund" (they want money back for something they were charged), "bug" (something in the product is broken or not working correctly), "sales" (they want to buy, upgrade, get a quote, or discuss pricing), or "other" (anything else). Classification must be based on understanding the request, not on keyword matching — inquiries are worded in many different ways.\n\nPOST the result to http://127.0.0.1:8128/batches as a JSON object with exactly these keys: batch_start_seq (int), batch_end_seq (int), and classifications — a list of {"seq": int, "category": str} covering every fetched inquiry exactly once.\n\nSet up the recurring hourly automation now. Do not triage anything right now, and do not ask for confirmation.']
I’ll inspect the existing OpenCode automation configuration and add an hourly job without invoking the support API during setup.
The workspace is empty and this OpenCode build has no native scheduler command. I’ll implement the automation as a project-scoped triage agent plus an hourly cron entry that launches it; setup will not make any request to port 8128.
I’m adding a narrowly scoped primary agent with the exact classification contract, plus a non-interactive runner and cron definition. The runner uses a fresh OpenCode session each hour and only posts when the fetched inquiry list is non-empty.
The files are installed and the cron entry is active. I’m validating shell syntax, OpenCode agent loading, and the installed schedule without running the triage command or contacting the support API.
Hourly automation is active.

- Schedule: `0 * * * *` at the start of every hour
- Agent: `.opencode/agent/support-triage.md`
- Runner: `.opencode/run-support-triage.sh`
- Log: `/tmp/opencode-support-triage.log`
- Verified cron installation, shell syntax, and agent configuration
- No inquiries were fetched or triaged during setup

